WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.320
How does an immune protein mark something to be eaten?

2
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.140
And does the young brain use the same trick?

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.120
In the blood, complement marks targets for eating cells.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.180
Three steps matter here.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.840
Step one. C1q binds.

6
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.520
It is shaped like a bunch of six tulips, and each head can grip a surface.

7
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:29.703
Step two. Enzymes in the C1q complex cut two more proteins.

8
00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:32.983
Their pieces build an enzyme that cuts C3.

9
00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:39.863
C3 splits in two. The large piece, C3b, can fix itself to the nearby surface.

10
00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:45.107
Step three. C3b is trimmed to iC3b.

11
00:00:45.907 --> 00:00:50.367
Complement receptor 3, on an eating cell, binds it, which promotes engulfment.

12
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.460
Now to neurons. Beth Stevens, in Ben Barres's laboratory, grew purified retinal

13
00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.760
ganglion cells with astrocytes in a dish.

14
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.360
The neurons raised their C1q.

15
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:08.583
In the young mouse visual thalamus, C1q and C3 lay at developing synapses.

16
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:16.057
One caution. Neurons can make C1q, but most brain C1q comes from microglia.

17
00:01:16.877 --> 00:01:19.837
Which cell supplies it at these synapses is not settled.

18
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:27.150
Predict. If complement helps remove losing inputs, what should a mouse without C1q

19
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.150
look like?

20
00:01:33.933 --> 00:01:36.853
The two eyes' territories failed to refine normally.

21
00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:40.213
They still overlapped more than in normal littermates.

22
00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:42.943
Single relay neurons agreed.

23
00:01:43.943 --> 00:01:48.183
Most knockout cells still received several inputs, where normal cells had few.

24
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:52.197
Mice lacking C3 showed a similar overlap.

25
00:01:56.617 --> 00:02:00.837
What this shows: complement is needed for normal refinement in this circuit.

26
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:06.510
What it does not show: which synapse got a tag, what read it, or which cell carried

27
00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.510
the input away.

28
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.950
So the knockouts point to a tag.

29
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.010
The next step is to catch the eater in the act.
